{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And YHWH caused to rain.</b> Wherever וַה' is stated — it is He and His court of justice." "<b>Caused to rain upon Sodom.</b> At the rising of dawn, as is stated ״וּכְמוֹ הַשַּׁחַר עָלָה״ — the hour when the moon stands in the firmament together with the sun, for some of them worshipped the sun and some of them the moon. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: If I exact punishment from them by day, the moon-worshippers will say, Had it been at night, when the moon rules, we would not have been destroyed; and if I exact punishment from them by night, the sun-worshippers will say, Had it been by day, when the sun rules, we would not have been destroyed. Therefore it is written ״וּכְמוֹ הַשַּׁחַר עָלָה״ — and He exacted punishment from them at the hour when the sun and the moon both rule." "<b>Caused to rain brimstone and fire.</b> At first it was rain, and it became brimstone and fire." "<b>From YHWH.</b> It is the way of Scripture to speak thus — like ״נְשֵׁי לֶמֶךְ,״ and it does not say נָשַׁי; and so David said ״קְחוּ עִמָּכֶם אֶת עַבְדֵי אֲדֹנֵיכֶם״ (I Kings 1), and he did not say מֵעֲבָדַי; and so Ahasuerus said ״בְּשֵׁם הַמֶּלֶךְ,״ and he did not say בִּשְׁמִי; so too here it says מֵאֵת ה' and does not say מֵאִתִּי." "<b>From the heavens.</b> This is what Scripture says: ״כִּי בָם יָדִין עַמִּים״ etc. (Job 36) — when He comes to chastise the creatures, He brings upon them fire from the heavens, as He did to Sodom; and when He comes to bring down the manna from the heavens: ״הִנְנִי מַמְטִיר לָכֶם לֶחֶם מִן הַשָּׁמַיִם״ (Exodus 16)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:36.002966929Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}